# Catalog tools and renderers

Catalog schema `1` supports three entry kinds: templates, external tool metadata, and renderer components. This page covers the two extension kinds; template source and override rules are in <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/catalog/templates">catalog templates</GuideRef>.

## Declare a metadata-only tool

<Example title="Advertise an external tool">

```toml
schema = "1"

[[entries]]
type = "tool"
id = "acme/architecture-tool"
command = "cargo-upwell-architecture"
description = "Checks Acme architecture policy"
package = "cargo-upwell-architecture"
protocols = ["upwell/axum", "upwell/rpc"]
```

</Example>

<Symbol path="cargo_upwell::init::catalog::ToolEntry" /> retains the command, description, optional package, and understood protocol IDs. In the validated inventory this is future integration metadata only: Cargo Upwell does not install or execute the command. Do not present a catalog tool entry as a supply-chain installer or plugin execution hook.

## Declare a renderer

```toml
[[entries]]
type = "renderer"
id = "acme/architecture-renderer"
component = "renderers/architecture.component.wasm"
commands = ["inspect", "graph"]
format = "architecture"
media-type = "text/plain"
extension = "txt"
color = false
pager = false
output-file = true
priority = 100
abi = "^0.1"
tooling-schema = "^0.20"
utf8 = true
```

`component` resolves relative to the catalog file. `commands` selects only commands whose canonical projection this component understands. `format` is command-scoped and must not collide with reserved built-in formats. `media-type`, optional extension, and capabilities control presentation policy; machine/binary formats cannot claim incompatible color, pager, or output behavior.

`abi` and `tooling-schema` are semantic-version requirements. Defaults come from the installed Cargo Upwell build, but writing them explicitly makes compatibility reviewable. Higher `priority` wins only among otherwise valid competing registrations; duplicate effective renderer/format/default rules are rejected by <Symbol path="cargo_upwell::renderer::RendererRegistry" />.

## Apply path and override rules

Catalog selection follows explicit path, environment path, then platform default. Relative component paths resolve from that selected file. Within one document, every ID is unique across all entry kinds. A tool or renderer cannot reuse a built-in or user template ID.

The exact platform defaults produced by `ProjectDirs::from("org", "upwell-rs", "Upwell")` are:

| Platform | Default catalog |
|---|---|
| macOS | `~/Library/Application Support/org.upwell-rs.Upwell/catalog.toml` |
| Linux | `${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/upwell/catalog.toml` |
| Windows | `%APPDATA%\upwell-rs\Upwell\config\catalog.toml` |

`cargo upwell templates` lists effective template IDs. Pass `--catalog <path>` to `templates`, `init`, or a renderer-capable command to inspect/use the same selected document; `UPWELL_CATALOG_PATH` applies to every Cargo Upwell command. Completion can expose catalog-backed renderer formats from metadata without loading or invoking the component.

User renderers combine with native built-ins. They do not replace canonical data production: Cargo Upwell prepares and validates the native command projection first, then passes a bounded payload to the selected renderer.

## Validate reproducibility and security

- Commit the catalog and component digest/release artifact together.
- Pin the renderer build toolchain and canonical WIT version.
- Keep component paths regular files; symlinks/reparse points and special files are rejected by platform checks.
- Do not rely on ambient working directory or a mutable global catalog in CI; pass `--catalog`.
- Preserve canonical JSON beside custom presentation when downstream automation needs lossless data.

<Callout type="warning" title="No host capabilities">

Renderer components must import nothing. They cannot read files, use the network, spawn processes, consult clocks through a host API, or execute catalog tools. Their entire input is the bounded render request.

</Callout>

## Troubleshoot extensions

- A tool entry appears in catalog output but does not run: expected; it is metadata-only.
- A renderer format is unavailable: verify command claim, catalog selector, registry validation, and semantic requirements.
- A component path works from one directory only: make it absolute or keep it relative to the catalog, not the shell.
- A duplicate ID may collide with an effective built-in template even when the user file declares only one entry.
- Binary output with `utf8 = true` is rejected if bytes are not UTF-8; set the contract deliberately.

Continue with <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/renderers/authoring">renderer authoring</GuideRef> and <GuideRef slug="cargo-upwell/renderers/testing-and-failures">renderer testing and failures</GuideRef>.
